1. What is Ansible?
• Ansible is an open-source automation tool for configuration management, application
deployment, and orchestration.
2. What are the key features of Ansible?
• Agentless, simple YAML syntax, idempotent operations, modular architecture.
3. What is an Ansible playbook?
• A YAML file containing a set of instructions (tasks) to automate configurations or
deployments.
4. What is an Ansible role?
• A structured way to organize playbooks, tasks, variables, templates, and files.
5. What is an Ansible inventory?
• A list of hosts and groups that Ansible manages, defined in INI or YAML format.
6. What is the difference between static and dynamic inventory in Ansible?
• Static: manually defined hosts.
• Dynamic: generated from a script or cloud source (e.g., AWS EC2).
7. How do you install Ansible on a Linux machine?
• Using sudo apt install ansible (Debian/Ubuntu) or sudo yum install ansible (RHEL/CentOS).
8. What is an Ansible module?
• A reusable unit of code in Ansible that performs a specific task (e.g., yum, apt, copy).
9. Name some common Ansible modules.
• file, copy, yum, apt, service, command, shell, user.
10. How do you run an Ansible playbook?
• ansible-playbook <playbook.yml>
11. How do you run an Ansible command on a single host?
• ansible <host> -m <module> -a "<args>"
12. What is idempotency in Ansible?
• Ensuring a task can run multiple times without changing the result after the first run.
13. How do you define variables in Ansible?
• Variables can be defined in playbooks, inventory, or external files (YAML).
14. What is an Ansible template?
• A Jinja2 file that can dynamically generate configuration files using variables.
15. How do you use loops in Ansible?
• Use loop or with_items to iterate over a list of values in a task.
16. What is an Ansible fact?
• Predefined information gathered from managed hosts, like OS, IP address, memory, etc.
17. How do you gather facts in Ansible?
• Use the setup module: ansible <host> -m setup
18. How do you skip fact gathering in a playbook?
• Set gather_facts: no at the start of the playbook.
19. What is a handler in Ansible?
• A task triggered by notify when another task changes, often used to restart services.
20. How do you notify a handler in Ansible?
• Add notify: <handler_name> under a task that should trigger it.
21. How do you include one playbook inside another?
• Use import_playbook or include directives in the main playbook.
22. How do you include tasks from another file?
• Use include_tasks or import_tasks in a playbook.
23. How do you define groups in Ansible inventory?
• Using [group_name] in INI format or groups: in YAML inventory.
24. How do you run Ansible on multiple hosts?
• Use -l <host_pattern> or define multiple hosts in inventory.
25. How do you pass variables at runtime?
• Use -e "var_name=value" when running the playbook.
26. How do you secure sensitive data in Ansible?
• Use Ansible Vault to encrypt variables or files.
27. How do you create a vault file?
